{
  "id": 2541,
  "title": "Please Don’t Open the Wrong Window",
  "russian_title": "Пожа́луйста, не откры́вайте не то око́но",
  "level": "Intermediate",
  "torfl_level": "A2",
  "hsk_tags": [
    "A2"
  ],
  "slug": "please-dont-open-the-wrong-window",
  "audio_url": "/audio/russian/2541_please-dont-open-the-wrong-window.mp3",
  "english_paragraphs": [
    "A little girl stood by the window, watching people outside bury their beloved puppy. The sight made her so sad that she began to cry.",
    "Her grandfather saw her and quickly led her to another window, where she could look out at a beautiful garden. The flowers were lovely, and sure enough, the little girl felt better as soon as she saw them. Before long, she was smiling happily. Her grandfather said, \"You were looking out the wrong window, my child. See? When you look out a different window, doesn't the world seem different?\"",
    "When you face failure, don't be too sad. Open the window beside it, and perhaps you'll find hope."
  ],
  "english_full": "A little girl stood by the window, watching people outside bury their beloved puppy. The sight made her so sad that she began to cry.\n\nHer grandfather saw her and quickly led her to another window, where she could look out at a beautiful garden. The flowers were lovely, and sure enough, the little girl felt better as soon as she saw them. Before long, she was smiling happily. Her grandfather said, \"You were looking out the wrong window, my child. See? When you look out a different window, doesn't the world seem different?\"\n\nWhen you face failure, don't be too sad. Open the window beside it, and perhaps you'll find hope.",
  "russian_paragraphs": [
    "Де́вочка стаяла у окна́ и смотри́ла, как лю́ди за́бывают своего люби́мого ку́тёнка. Вид мог за́грустить её, и она́ нача́ла плака́ть.",
    "Её де́душка у́видел её и бы́стро привёл её к друго́му око́ну, откуда она́ могла́ смотри́ть на краси́вый сад. Цветы́ бы́ли восхити́тельными, и, как ни́ в чём не бы́ло, де́вочка на́конец чувстовала́ себя́ лу́чше, как то́лько она́ их уви́дела. Не про́шло и много́ вре́мени, как она́ начина́ла улы́баться сча́стливо. Её де́душка ска́зал: «Ты смотри́ла из не того о́кна, моё дитя́. Ви́дешь? Когда́ ты смотри́шь из друго́го око́на, мир не казáтся другим?»",
    "Когда́ ты стои́шь перед неуда́чей, не бы́вай сли́шком гру́стным. Открой окно́ ря́дом, и возмо́жно, ты на́дешь надежду."
  ],
  "reading_paragraphs": [
    "Dévochka stála u okná i smotríla, kak lyúdi zabývayut svoego lyubímogo kuténka. Vid mog zágrustít' yéy, i oná nachála plakát'.",
    "Yéyo dédushka uývidél yéy i býstro privyól yéy k drugómu okná, otkuda oná moglá smotrít' na krasívyy sad. Tsvetý býli voskhitítel'nymi, i, kak nì v chém ne býlo, dévochka nákonets' chuvstvovalá sebá lúchshe, kak tó'l'ko oná ikh uvídela. Ne próshlo i mnógo vrémeni, kak oná nachínala ulýbát'sya schástitel'no. Yéyo dédushka skázal: 'Ty smotríla iz ne tógo okná, moyé dít'ya. Vídesh? Kogdá ty smotrísh' iz drugógo okná, mir ne kazátsya drugím?'",
    "Kogdá ty stoísh' peréd neudachéy, ne bývay slýshkom grústnym. Otkroy oknó ryádom, i vozmózhno, ty náydesh' nadézhdu."
  ],
